"{\n  \"reasoning\": \"Power limit gives Itail \u226415\u202f\u00b5A (2\u00b7Itail\u00b73.3\u202fV \u2264100\u202f\u00b5W). To meet GBW \u22655\u202fMHz with CL=5\u202fpF, gm1 \u22652\u03c0\u00b75e6\u00b75e-12 \u2248157\u202f\u00b5S. Using Id = Itail/2 and gm\u22482\u00b7Id/Vov, choose Vov1\u22480.09\u202fV, giving gm\u2248167\u202f\u00b5S with Itail=15\u202f\u00b5A. This sets (W/L)\u22489.3 for NMOS; with L1=0.5\u202f\u00b5m, W1\u22484.6\u202f\u00b5m. Long channel (L=0.5\u202f\u00b5m) reduces \u03bb, giving gds low enough for A0\u2248gm1/(gds2+gds4) >45\u202fdB. Tail NMOS sized for Itail=15\u202f\u00b5A and Vov5\u22480.2\u202fV gives W5\u22481.9\u202f\u00b5m (L5=0.5\u202f\u00b5m). PMOS load sized for the same current with Vov4\u22480.3\u202fV gives (W/L)\u22483.3; with L3=0.5\u202f\u00b5m, W3\u22481.7\u202f\u00b5m. Output swing \u22483.3\u2011Vov4\u2011Vtail\u2011Vov1 \u22482.7\u202fV >1.5\u202fV. Mirror pole is pushed above GBW by modest node capacitance, ensuring \u226560\u00b0 phase margin.\",\n  \"W1_um\": 4.6,\n  \"L1_um\": 0.5,\n  \"W3_um\": 1.7,\n  \"L3_um\": 0.5,\n  \"W5_um\": 1.9,\n  \"L5_um\": 0.5,\n  \"Itail_uA\": 15\n}"